lude `thread.id`, so the plugin does not rely on it for session identity.\n36: \n37: ## Session Management\n38: - Session ID source: Amp `thread.id`.\n39: - Session directory: `.entire/tmp/amp/`.\n40: - Session file format: JSONL cache written by the external agent binary from hook payloads.\n41: - Resume mechanism: `PLUGINS=all amp threads continue <thread-id>`.\n42: \n43: ## Transcript\n44: - Location: `.entire/tmp/amp/<safe-thread-id>.jsonl`.\n45: - Format: JSONL with `agent.start` and `agent.end` entries.\n46: - User prompt field: `agent.start.message`.\n47: - Modified files field: `agent.end.modified_files`, populated via `amp.helpers.filesModifiedByToolCall`.\n48: - Token usage field: unavailable in documented plugin events.\n49: \n50: ## Protocol Mapping\n51: | Subcommand | Native Concept | Implementation Notes | Feasibility |\n52: |-----------|----------------|----------------------|-------------|\n53: | `info` | static metadata | Return name `amp`, capabilities | Required |\n54: | `detect` | `amp` binary | Check `command -v amp` | Required |\n55: | `get-session-id` | Amp thread ID | Read from hook input | Required |\n56: | `get-session-dir` | `.entire/tmp` | Standard Entire temp dir | Required |\n57: | `resolve-session-file` | `.entire/tmp/<id>.json` | Standard path resolution | Required |\n58: | `read-session` | cached JSONL | Build AgentSession from cache | Required |\n59: | `write-session` | cached JSONL | Write native data to session ref | Required |\n60: | `read-transcript` | cached JSONL | Return raw bytes | Required |\n61: | `chunk-transcript` | raw bytes | Base64 chunking via protocol JSON encoding | Required |\n62: | `reassemble-transcript` | chunks | Reassemble raw bytes | Required |\n63: | `format-resume-command` | Amp thread continue | `PLUGINS=all amp threads continue <id>` | Required |\n64: | `parse-hook` | plugin event JSON | Map hook payloads to protocol events | Hooks |\n65: | `install-hooks` | project plugin | Write `.amp/plugins/entire.ts` | Hooks |\n66: | `uninstall-hooks` | project plugin | Remove `.amp/plugins/entire.ts` | Hooks |\n67: | `are-hooks-installed` | project plugin | Check plugin marker | Hooks |\n68: | `get-transcript-position` | JSONL line count | Return line count offset | Transcript analyzer |\n69: | `extract-modified-files` | plugin helper output | Read `modified_files` arrays | Transcript analyzer |\n70: | `extract-prompts` | `agent.start` entries | Read prompt text | Transcript analyzer |\n71: | `extract-summary` | last assistant text | Read last assistant text block from `agent.end.messages` | Transcript analyzer |\n72: | `compact-transcript` | cached messages | Emit Entire compact JSONL | Compact transcript |\n73: \n74: ## Selected Capabilities\n75: | Capability | Declared | Justification |\n76: |-----------|----------|---------------|\n77: | hooks | true | Amp plugins expose lifecycle events |\n78: | transcript_analyzer | true | Plugin captures enough prompt/message/file data |\n79: | compact_transcript | true | Captured messages map to Entire compact transcript format |\n80: | transcript_preparer | false | Cache is directly readable |\n81: | token_calculator | false | Token usage is not documented in plugin events |\n82: | text_generator | false | Amp CLI is used for agent execution, not summary generation |\n83: | hook_response_writer | false | Not needed for lifecycle hooks |\n84: | subagent_aware_extractor | false | No documented subagent transcript tree |\n85: \n86: ## Gaps & Limitations\n87: - Amp must be launched with `PLUGINS=all` for hooks to fire.\n88: - Transcript data is plugin-captured, not a documented native Amp session file.\n89: - Token usage is not available from documented plugin event payloads.\n90: - `session.start` cannot be trusted for thread identity because `thread.id` is optional there.\n91: \n92: ## E2E Test Prerequisites\n93: - Entire CLI binary: `entire` from PATH or `E2E_ENTIRE_BIN`.\n94: - Agent CLI binary: `amp`.\n95: - Non-interactive prompt c