              "plan": "**Plan: Make Amp Exported Thread JSON Authoritative**\n\n**Goal**\n- Treat the `amp threads export <thread-id>` JSON document as the authoritative session/transcript payload for `entire-agent-amp` protocol behavior.\n- Use `internal/amp/types.go` (`AmpThread`, `ThreadMessage`, `ThreadContentBlock`, `ThreadUsage`, etc.) as the parser model for prepared transcripts.\n- Keep plugin JSONL only as a short-lived bootstrap format used to discover the Amp thread ID before `prepare-transcript` exports the authoritative JSON.\n\n**Current Problem**\n- `transcript.go` currently uses ad hoc `threadMessage` / `contentBlock` structs and generic recursive JSON probing for prepared JSON.\n- Protocol methods can still satisfy requests from plugin JSONL, which conflicts with the requirement that exported Amp thread JSON be authoritative.\n- `compact.go` also uses the ad hoc structs, so compact transcript generation is not based on `types.go`.\n- `CalculateTokens` is still a stub even though `types.go` models `ThreadUsage` from exported transcripts.\n\n**Implementation Strategy**\n- Introduce a small transcript loader that reads `sessionRef` and returns either:\n  - a parsed `AmpThread` from exported JSON, or\n  - a minimal plugin JSONL bootstrap record only for `PrepareTranscript` to locate `thread_id`.\n- Remove generic prepared-JSON probing (`findThreadID`, `findThreadMessages`, `decodeThreadMessages`) from protocol paths.\n- Update all post-prepare protocol methods to parse `AmpThread` directly using `json.Unmarshal` into `AmpThread`.\n- If a non-prepare protocol method receives plugin JSONL instead of exported JSON, return a clear error instructing that `prepare-transcript` must run first, except where Entire needs bootstrap behavior before preparation.\n\n**Protocol Behavior After Refactor**\n- `PrepareTranscript(sessionRef)`:\n  - Read plugin JSONL from `sessionRef`.\n  - Extract `thread_id` from bootstrap hook entries.\n  - Run `CommandRunner.ExportThread(ctx, threadID, sessionRef)`.\n  - The resulting `sessionRef` now contains authoritative Amp thread JSON.\n- `ReadSession(input)`:\n  - Parse `sessionRef` as `AmpThread`.\n  - Use `AmpThread.ID` as `SessionID`.\n  - Use `AmpThread.Created` / `UpdatedAt` for `StartTime` where appropriate.\n  - Store the raw exported JSON as `NativeData`.\n  - Use exported thread messages to compute `ModifiedFiles`.\n- `ReadTranscript(sessionRef)`:\n  - Return raw exported JSON bytes.\n- `GetTranscriptPosition(path)`:\n  - For exported JSON, return byte length or a stable unit compatible with downstream offsets; prefer byte length because the protocol says byte offset for transcript analyzer.\n- `ExtractPrompts(sessionRef, offset)`:\n  - Parse `AmpThread.Messages` and extract user text blocks from `ThreadMessageRoleUser` messages.\n  - Ignore plugin JSONL except in tests specific to `PrepareTranscript`.\n- `ExtractSummary(sessionRef)`:\n  - Parse `AmpThread.Messages` and use the last assistant text block from `ThreadMessageRoleAssistant`.\n- `ExtractModifiedFiles(path, offset)`:\n  - Parse `AmpThread.Messages` and extract file paths from authoritative Amp structures.\n  - Prefer `ThreadToolRun.TrackFiles` from `tool_result` blocks when present.\n  - Also inspect tool-use `ThreadToolInput` fields like `path`, `filePath`, `files`, and common result fields like `absolutePath` if needed.\n- `CompactTranscript(sessionRef)`:\n  - Parse `AmpThread` and convert `ThreadMessage` / `ThreadContentBlock` to Entire compact transcript JSONL.\n  - Use `ThreadMessage.MessageID`, `ThreadMessage.Meta.SentAt`, `ThreadUsage.InputTokens`, and `ThreadUsage.OutputTokens` where available.\n  - Inline tool results by matching `ThreadContentToolResult.ToolUseID` to preceding `ThreadContentToolUse.ID`.\n- `CalculateTokens(data, offset)`:\n  - Parse `AmpThread` from the provided transcript bytes.\n  - Sum `ThreadUsage.InputTokens`, `OutputTokens`, `CacheReadInputTokens`, `CacheCreationInputTokens`, and count messages with usage.\n  - Consider enabling `token_calculator: true` in `Info()` once tests pass.\n\n**Types And Conversions**\n- Use `ThreadMessageRoleUser`, `ThreadMessageRoleAssistant`, `ThreadContentText`, `ThreadContentToolUse`, and `ThreadContentToolResult` constants instead of string literals.\n- Add helper methods/functions if needed:\n  - `ThreadUnixMillis.Time() time.Time` or local converter for `SentAt` / `Created`.\n  - `threadMessageIDString(ThreadMessageID) string`.\n  - `threadToolInputValue(input ThreadToolInput, keys ...string) []string`.\n  - `threadToolRunOutput(run *ThreadToolRun) string` using `ThreadCommonToolResult`.\n- Keep helpers small and local to parsing/compact files unless they naturally belong with `types.go`.\n\n**Tests To Add/Update**\n- Replace prepared JSON fixtures in tests with an `AmpThread`-shaped fixture matching `types.go`, including:\n  - top-level `v`, `id`, `created`, `updatedAt`, and `messages`.\n  - user text message.\n  - assistant message with `tool_use`, text, and `usage`.\n  - user/tool-result block with `run.trackFiles` and result output.\n- Update tests so protocol extraction/summary/compact/token tests use exported Amp JSON, not ad hoc generic JSON.\n- Keep one plugin JSONL fixture solely for `PrepareTranscript` thread ID extraction.\n- Add a test that extraction methods return an error for unprepared plugin JSONL to enforce the authoritative-export requirement.\n- Add token calculation tests from `ThreadUsage` and update `Info` tests if `token_calculator` is enabled.\n- Add/adjust compact transcript assertions for `ThreadMessage.MessageID`, token fields, tool input, and inlined tool result output/status.\n\n**Validation**\n- Run `gofmt` on changed Go files.\n- Run `go test ./...` in `agents/entire-agent-amp`.\n- Build with `go build -o entire-agent-amp ./cmd/entire-agent-amp`.\n- Run `external-agents-tests verify ./entire-agent-amp`.\n- Compile the e2e harness if public protocol capability declarations change."
