`agent.start`                                                     | TurnStart (type 2)    |\n43: | `agent.end`                                                       | TurnEnd (type 3)      |\n44: \n45: Amp threads are server-side, so the plugin payloads are cached as JSONL under `.entire/tmp/amp/<thread-id>.jsonl`. When Entire calls `prepare-transcript`, the binary replaces that cache with the JSON output from `amp threads export <thread-id>` for later parsing.\n46: \n47: ## Development\n48: \n49: ```bash\n50: go build -o entire-agent-amp ./cmd/entire-agent-amp\n51: go test ./...\n52: external-agents-tests verify ./entire-agent-amp\n53: \n54: cd ../../\n55: E2E_AGENT=amp mise run test:e2e\n56: ```\n\n(End of file - total 56 lines)\n</content>",
